# ── Discord integration (server-only) ──────────────────────────
# Everything here is read ONLY by server code (lib/discord.js, API
# routes). NEVER prefix these with NEXT_PUBLIC_ and NEVER import
# them into client components — `import "server-only"` enforces this
# at build time.
#
# Setup (one time, owner only):
#   1. https://discord.com/developers → New Application → OAuth2.
#   2. Add a redirect URL exactly matching DISCORD_REDIRECT_URI, e.g.
#      https://your-domain.vercel.app/api/auth/discord/callback
#      (local: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/discord/callback)
#   3. Set the four variables below, redeploy, open /setup/discord
#      (unlinked route), authorize (identify scope only).
#   4. Save the displayed refresh token as DISCORD_REFRESH_TOKEN,
#      redeploy once more. Done — visitors never log in.

# Public identifier of your Discord application (not a secret, but
# keep it server-side with the rest for a clean boundary).
# DISCORD_CLIENT_ID=

# OAuth client secret — SECRET. Server env only, never commit.
# DISCORD_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Must match a redirect URL registered in the Discord portal.
# DISCORD_REDIRECT_URI=

# Owner refresh token from the one-time setup flow — SECRET.
# Runtime mints short-lived access tokens from this; the access
# token itself is never stored, logged, or sent to the browser.
# DISCORD_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# Resolves the site owner's account. Public constant, safe here.
# DISCORD_USER_ID=920627516694200360
